From a99456f53cbe845b712b1389dbcd136b9c6ce842 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Slava Tutrinov <slava@tutrinov.pro>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:51:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] [SDPOZN] Audit: Elasticsearch low-level REST client 8.19.8,
 httpcomponents 4.5.14/4.4.16

ElasticSearchAuditDestination now uses only elasticsearch-rest-client 8.19.8
(Java 8 bytecode) and builds the _bulk NDJSON body itself with Gson. The
document format is the same as the old XContent output (UTC
yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss.SSSZ dates, nulls kept, sets as arrays).

The Elasticsearch server jar, the high-level client, x-content and the
module clients are no longer pulled by ranger-plugins-audit nor packaged in
plugin assemblies, which removes CVE-2025-37731, CVE-2025-37727 and the
older server-side Elasticsearch CVEs from every plugin package. Ranger
Admin and the embedded web server keep the 7.17 high-level client
explicitly (no 8.x release of it exists).

httpclient/httpmime 4.5.14, httpcore(-nio) 4.4.16, httpasyncclient 4.1.5:
fixes CVE-2020-13956 and matches what the 8.19.8 REST client is built with.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
